# Managed by the website repo (ops/caddy/umami.caddy, #948). ops/install-umami.sh fills in the host
# and port, copies the result to /etc/caddy/sprecher-east-umami.caddy and imports it from
# the Caddyfile, but only after Umami's default admin password has been replaced. Change it in
# the repo, not on the server.
#
# Umami has its own address because the prebuilt image cannot run under a path (BASE_PATH is
# fixed when the image is built). Caddy gets the certificate and redirects plain HTTP by itself.
# The HSTS rule is the site's own file (ops/caddy/hsts.caddy), so there is one definition of it.
__UMAMI_HOST__ {
	import /etc/caddy/sprecher-east-hsts.caddy
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:__UMAMI_PORT__
}
